#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/weighted.rst:12
#: c483b089d24947fe9cd7cc449b530598
msgid ""
"A **weighted graph** is a graph where each edge has an associated numeric"
" value called a **weight**. Weights typically represent costs, distances,"
" capacities, or other quantitative relationships between nodes. Weighted "
"graphs are fundamental for modeling real-world networks where connections"
" have varying strengths or costs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/weighted.rst:38
#: 876cff1434de41baac8f9b4d22809614
msgid ""
"Weighted graphs enable sophisticated analysis like shortest path "
"algorithms (Dijkstra, Bellman-Ford), minimum spanning trees (Kruskal, "
"Prim), and network flow optimization that are impossible with unweighted "
"graphs."
msgstr ""

